comments:
Good catch @brunnerh. It looks like any attempt to set the value of a property of an object in an `#each` block, is essentially ignoring anything other than the root and leaf variable names.

Adding a button into the `#each` block like this:
```
<button on:click={()=>{
	person.name.first = "dave";
	person.first = "dave";
	person.a.really.long.path.to.first = "dave";
	people = people;
}}>person.name.first = "dave"</button>
```
Is compiled into:
```
var on_click = (_, person, people) => {
	$.unwrap(person).first = "dave";
	$.unwrap(person).first = "dave";
	$.unwrap(person).first = "dave";
	$.set(people, $.get(people));
};
```
Since this is a more general issue than I originally described, I will edit this issue to clarify all this.
